#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Generated by dx images sync from dx/scripts/images. Do not edit; change dx and re-run sync.
"""Validate and extend the image registry (images.config).

Every third-party container image pinned in any Qualithm repo has one entry in
images.config, as <repo>:<exact tag>@sha256:<multi-arch index digest>
(Decision qualithm/pm#744, amendment 2026-10-03).

Usage:
  images verify [--config FILE] [--offline] [ref ...]
  images pin <repo>:<tag> ...
  images check [--config FILE] [--json] [repo-or-path ...]
  images sync [--dry-run] [--no-pr] [repo-or-path ...]
  images drift [repo ...]

`verify` proves each entry is safe to pin before sync copies it anywhere. Each
finding carries a stable code:

  error  bad-line          the line is not <repo>:<tag>@sha256:<digest> [waiver]
  error  latest            the tag is `latest`
  error  duplicate-flavor  two entries pin the same image flavor
                           (e.g. two rust:<v>-alpine<v>)
  error  digest-missing    the digest does not exist in the repository
  error  not-index         the digest is a single-platform or attestation
                           manifest, not a multi-arch index
  error  no-amd64          the index has no linux/amd64 image
  error  tag-missing       the tag no longer exists
  error  tag-moves         a more specific tag points at the same digest
                           (2.15-scratch when 2.15.0-scratch is the same image)
  error  unreachable       the registry could not be queried
  warn   no-arm64          the index has no linux/arm64 image (local development
                           on Apple silicon)
  warn   tag-rebuilt       the tag now points at a different digest; upstream
                           rebuilt it. Bumping stays a human call, and the weekly
                           image audit reports it.

--offline runs only the checks that need no network. Refs or image names on the
command line limit the online checks to those entries. Exit 1 on any error that
is not waived.

`pin` prints the registry line for a tag. It resolves the tag's multi-arch index
digest and, when a more specific tag points at the same image, pins that tag
instead (alpine:3.24 -> alpine:3.24.2@sha256:...). Use it to add or bump an
entry. Exit 1 when a tag cannot be resolved.

`check` finds every image reference in a repo and holds it to the registry.
With no arguments it checks every repo in repos.json under $QUALITHM_ROOT
(default: dx's parent directory); an argument is a repo name or a path. It reads:

  Dockerfile*, Containerfile*, *.Dockerfile  FROM, COPY --from, RUN --mount from=,
                                             with ARG defaults substituted
  compose files                              services.*.image (anchors resolved,
                                             ${VAR:-default} substituted); a
                                             service with `build:` is skipped
  Helm charts                                every image field and image-like
                                             string in `helm template` output, for
                                             values.yaml layered with every
                                             values-<env>, values-<az> and
                                             values-<env>-<az> combination, plus
                                             repository/tag pins in values files
                                             that no combination renders
  workflows and actions                      container, services.*.image,
                                             docker:// uses
  other YAML                                 `image:` lines
  code (.ts .tsx .js .mjs .go .rs .py)       quoted image references
  Markdown code fences                       docker run/pull/create, FROM, image:
  every other text file                      docker run/pull/create

Each reference yields at most one finding:

  error  unresolved            a variable the check cannot resolve
  error  no-tag                no tag (a digest alone is unreadable and untracked)
  error  no-digest             the registry's tag, but no digest
  error  mismatch              differs from the registry entry for that flavor
  error  unregistered          the image (or this flavor of it) has no entry
  error  first-party-unpinned  ghcr.io/qualithm/* without tag and digest
  error  render-failed         no values combination of a chart renders
  error  tool-missing          helm or yq is not installed
  info   allowed               matched an allow line
  warn   allow-unused          an allow line matched nothing (whole-fleet runs)

A reference that must differ from the registry (a locally built image, a test
fixture) is listed in images.config as
`allow <repo> <path-glob> <reference> <reason>`; the reason is required.
Exit 1 on any error.

`sync` propagates the registry. For each repo in images-sync.config (or each
argument) it rewrites every reference that differs from its registry entry,
whether a literal in a Dockerfile, compose file, workflow, YAML, Markdown or
code, or a Helm values pin (a repository/tag/digest map, a subchart tag field
carrying tag@digest, or a full-reference override). It then vendors the registry
and this script into .github/images/, which the CI Image Pins job runs. It
commits on an images-sync branch cut from the repo's integration branch and
opens the PR with `dx git feature`. It never edits the registry: bumping stays a
human change to images.config. A reference it cannot rewrite safely (a variable,
a subchart default with no values pin) prints as `manual`. --dry-run works on a
copy and prints what would change; --no-pr edits the working tree only.

`drift` exits 1 when an enrolled repo's vendored files are missing or stale, or
when a repo that references images is not enrolled.

A known violation that another board issue removes is waived on its entry, never
silently: `waive=<code>[,<code>] issue=<owner>/<repo>#<n>`. A waived finding
still prints, as `waived`, and does not fail the run.

Registries are reached over their HTTP API with anonymous bearer tokens, so no
docker, crane or skopeo is needed. A registry host of localhost or 127.0.0.1 is
spoken to over plain HTTP (used by images-test).
"""
